title: $:/Lithic/Patches/Whiteboard/MobileViewport
tags: $:/tags/Stylesheet
type: text/css

/* A phone's browser draws its own chrome over the page, so 100vh is the
   viewport with that chrome hidden, not the one the reader can see. The board
   is sized in vh: the page layout passes height="100vh" to the whiteboard
   widget, which writes it as an inline height on .tw-whiteboard-tldraw-container,
   and tldraw anchors its bottom toolbar to the bottom of that box. On a phone
   the box therefore runs on under the browser chrome, the toolbar is anchored
   below the visible area, and no tool is reachable until the page is scrolled.

   dvh is the viewport that is actually on screen, so the box ends where the
   reader's screen ends and the toolbar arrives with it. The vh line stays in
   front of the dvh line for engines that have no dvh, and !important is the
   only way to reach a height the widget set inline. Scoped to a coarse
   pointer, so a desktop window keeps its 100vh. */

@media (pointer: coarse) {
    .tw-whiteboard-tldraw-container {
        height: 100vh !important;
        height: 100dvh !important;
    }
}